      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "\"Quality Realtime interpolation\"\n-------------------------------\n\nBenefit from the prompting capabilities and the speed of SDXL Turbo combined with the SD1.5 LCM LoRA and a 1.5 model to get decent quality images in 0.6 seconds on an RTX 3090. Enable \"Extra Options\" and then \"Auto Queue\" for \"realtime\" interpolations!\n\nMultiple \"Blending Modes\" are available, so play with them all! Want to turn a cat into a rodent (and let's face it, who doesn't)? Enter \"cat\" in Prompt A, \"rodent\" in Prompt B, select \"bislerp\" blending mode and then change the Blending Strength. Exclusion is the only one that doesn't really work.\n\nYou can change prompts in realtime too for even more fun! Note that max prompt token lengths should match for Prompt A and Prompt B (e.g. 77 or 154 in each, etc)\n\nNote that images aren't saved by default as you'd get a lot - plus they're in your temp directory already. Note that if you are changing the final image node from a preview to a save node, remember to include the word \"Detailed\" (or update the image regex).\n\nInspired by this post on reddit - https://t.co/d3UuEVwBFV"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
